abstract: >-
  Decode microbenchmarks of llama.cpp speculative decoding for
  Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_XL on one RTX 3090. The archival tier was collected
  between 2026-04-21 and 2026-05-07 at llama.cpp commits 97895129e, bcb5eeb64
  and PR-branch 67cb0d507, one run per cell. A controlled tier collected on
  2026-08-25/26 at commit 3737e4137 adds repeated arm-runs with matched
  no-speculation baselines, verified thinking suppression, recorded concurrent
  client-request windows, per-request text and token ids, and continuous GPU
  telemetry. Four further runs on 2026-08-27 and 2026-08-28 at the same commit
  add a between-invocation crossover (V2, 400 arm-runs), a within-invocation
  Latin square (V3, 200), a checkpoint split-timer probe (T4, 18) and a
  within-invocation 10x10 Williams square with randomised row order (W, 500),
  which together revise the archival tier's headline: under this controlled
  design DFlash n-max 2 and MTP n-max 2 exceed the no-speculation baseline on
  this card, while an external Qwen3.5-0.8B draft model falls well below it. The harness records how many client requests were outstanding at
  once, which is not the same as the number of sequences sharing a server
  decode graph. The repository preserves per-request timings and the SHA-256 of
  every raw server log, and an audit (ERRATA.md) documenting which of the
  originally published claims survive re-examination and which do not; the raw
  controlled-tier logs are published as release assets and the extraction
  is re-runnable from them. Findings are bounded to
  llama.cpp commit 3737e4137 and the recorded configuration.
